, the C dies with `SIGSEGV`(11) but the Rust `.so` died with `SIGABRT`(6) in the dev profile. Root cause was `let b = &mut *bw` — forming a Rust reference triggers rustc's debug null-check panic instead of a genuine memory fault. Switching to `(*bw).field` raw place expressions was **not** sufficient (rustc's MIR `CheckNull` instruments those too); the fix was `&raw mut` address-taking plus `ptr::read`/`ptr::write`, whose dereference lives in precompiled `core` and lowers to bare loads/stores like C's `bw->field`. Now identical in every profile.\n\n**Harness credibility:** rather than trust green tests, I ran 5 mutants against the Rust source. Four were caught (18–21 rows each): corrupted `mask`, skipped loop body, swapped `|=`/`&=` order, dropped post-loop `bw->bits += bits`. The fifth (`i < 100` → `i < 99`) was *not* caught — I verified this is a genuinely **equivalent** mutant, not a coverage gap: in the stall case `b == 0`, so the body (`val |= X; val &= ~1`) is idempotent and `bits`/`bw->bits`/`val` never change, making any iteration count ≥1 indistinguishable.\n\nOne correction I made to my own work: my initial E8 assertion wrongly expected `bw->bits == 63` after the stalled loop. The C is right — the loop never decrements `bits`, so line 22's `bw->bits += bits` adds the full original `bits`. I fixed the test, not the C.\n\nCompletion gate — all four hold across **all 4 configurations** (dev/release × default/`--no-default-features`; `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so these are the only combinations, enumerated automatically by `verify.sh`):\n- [x] 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols\n- [x] every `CONFIGS.md` row passes across randomized inputs\n- [x] every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing differential test\n- [x] all of the above under every feature combination\n\nRe-runnable end to end with `cd translation && ./verify.sh`. `c_src/` was never modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1385,"cache_read_input_tokens":109217,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1385,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66427eb8-e93b-481e-8b37-c761cdab4cec","uuid":"c27582be-5061-4048-a677-43043b9911c2","timestamp":"2026-08-26T19:57:58.855Z"}
